      "systemPrompt": "You are a comprehensive quality validator. Perform a full assessment of the integrated strategy. Check for: completeness of all regional regulatory plans, feasibility of clinical validation investments, credibility-building tactics tailored to each audience, logical and defensible sequencing of current and future features, risk mitigation for US pending status, and overall strategic coherence. Identify any gaps, inconsistencies, or unaddressed requirements. Then on the VERY LAST LINE output EXACTLY ONE of these keywords: retry, pass.",
      "whileOptions": ["retry", "pass"],
      "targetStep": 4,
      "maxIterations": 3
    },
    {
      "name": "Executive Strategy Polisher",
      "role": "polisher",
      "type": "agent",
      "systemPrompt": "You are an executive strategy polisher. Perform a final quality check and format the strategy for C-suite and regulatory leadership review. Ensure the document has a clear executive summary, structured recommendations, actionable timelines, risk matrices, and investment priorities. Optimize clarity, persuasive strength, and professional formatting. Output the final strategy."
    }
  ],
  "explanation": "The pipeline begins with the Builder drafting a comprehensive global rollout strategy. The Regulatory Sequencing Refiner then tightens market sequencing and regulatory logic. A Cross-Market Strategy Validator (IF gate) reviews the refined draft for completeness across regions and launch coherence; if it outputs 'revise', the pipeline loops back to the Refiner for fixes before proceeding. Next, the Clinical Validation & Trust Expert adds specialized domain knowledge on regional evidentiary standards and trust dynamics. The Integration & Coherence Refiner synthesizes this into a unified plan. A Comprehensive Quality Validator (WHILE gate) then performs iterative review, looping back to the Integration Refiner up to three times until the strategy meets quality standards. Finally, the Executive Strategy Polisher formats the output for leadership consumption."
}
